Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:25:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/36] ggml-hexagon co-op reading: the CPU pre-quantizes the
 NPU share's input (q8_K/q8_0 into the NPU layout, compute-usage buffer so the
 NPU drops stale cache lines), reuses it for gate/up and q/k, groups CPU ops
 into one graph, keeps a full CPU copy so batches under LG_COOP_MIN (32) run
 CPU-only; persona reading 31 -> 35 tok/s in the server, KL 0.0036 (CPU-only
 path bit-identical)

